# Phase 8: Recurrent Hybrid Architecture (Wilson-Cowan + LSTM)

You observed the incredible forecasting power of the LSTM natively parsing sliding sequences, and have accurately identified the final conceptual frontier: **Merging the physiological constraints of the Mechanistic ODE strictly with the recurrent sequential memory of an LSTM!**

By replacing the feedforward MLP `residual_net` with an `LSTM`, the Hybrid model will no longer simply guess residual drifts from a single snapshot of time. Instead, the LSTM will maintain a deep contextual sequence memory of the entire trajectory, deploying highly context-aware adjustments to the ODE equations strictly when the physics boundaries require correction over time.

### Implementation Blueprint

1. **Refactor `HybridModel` Initialization:**
   - Remove the `nn.Sequential` feedforward MLP layers.
   - Inject a dedicated `nn.LSTMCell(input_size=3, hidden_size=64)` to process the $[E_{curr}, I_{curr}, u_t]$ inputs sequentially.
   - Initialize a residual projection layer `nn.Linear(64, 2)` to map the hidden state to $[dE_{res}, dI_{res}]$.
   - Initialize the projection layer weights to exactly zero (`nn.init.zeros_`) so the architecture begins entirely mathematically equivalent to the raw Wilson-Cowan baseline at Epoch 0!

2. **Update the `forward` Sequence Tracking loop:**
   - Track $h_t$ and $c_t$ systematically across the continuous mapping.
   - Natively extract $x_{curr}$ identically from the `x_seq` sliding window to supply perfect sequential momentum into the equations without breaking the continuous integration!

3. **Modify the `step` Integrator:**
   - Instead of the MLP firing 5 separate times inside the micro-stepping block independently, the LSTM will update its hidden state precisely once per macroscopic data frame interval, holding the physical residual constraint $d_{res}$ constant during the 5 micro-Euler iterations to ensure mathematical stability and prevent LSTM state-collapse!

4. **Runner Configuration:**
   - Add `HybridModel` back into `run_experiment.py` targeting the new LSTM-augmented class.
   - Re-run the lightweight validation loop to benchmark the Hybrid + LSTM against the Pure LSTM.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Modifying the internal states of the Mechanistic Micro-stepping loop to support contiguous recurrent memories is a major architectural adjustment. 
> Do you approve this precise implementation plan to structurally swap the Hybrid residual core to an LSTM architecture?
